Since you have sample imbalances across your species, and you want your PCA shape not to be biased towards species with more samples, an easier solution would be fitting GPA (without scaling) for each species individually, and feeding the consensus shapes from those into your final shape analysis and PCA decomposition. In your final analysis, by definition each species (with multiple samples) will be represented by their species means.

